# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the real one.
#
# Local development needs none of this: with DATABASE_URL unset the platform
# runs on ./musanga.db with nothing to install.

# --- database -------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase gives you this under Project settings -> Database -> Connection
# string. Copy the *pooler* URI and paste it whole, password and all.
#
# Use the pooler, not the direct host: Supabase serves direct connections over
# IPv6 only, and neither Vercel nor most CI runners have outbound IPv6.
#
# Port 5432 on the pooler is session mode, which is what this app wants - the
# driver uses prepared statements, and transaction mode (6543) recycles the
# connection underneath them.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# verify (default) checks the server certificate against the CA below.
# no-verify still encrypts but stops proving who answered. disable turns TLS
# off entirely and should never be used against Supabase.
# MUSANGA_DB_SSL=verify

# Supabase's endpoints are signed by their own CA, not a public one. The root
# is already committed at supabase/prod-ca.crt, so this needs no setup. Point
# it elsewhere only if you keep the certificate somewhere else.
# MUSANGA_DB_CA=supabase/prod-ca.crt

# How many Postgres connections this process keeps open. Keep it small on
# serverless, where every instance holds its own.
# MUSANGA_DB_POOL=5

# --- app ------------------------------------------------------------------
# production turns on long asset caching, HSTS, and generic error messages.
MUSANGA_ENV=production
HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=8080

# How long a sign-in lasts, in seconds. Default 14 days.
# MUSANGA_SESSION_DAYS=14

# Loads demo data on an EMPTY database only. Every demo account shares one
# published password, so leave this unset for anything real.
# MUSANGA_SEED=demo

# --- optional: Supabase REST (musanga/store.py) ----------------------------
# Not used by the platform, which talks SQL directly. Only needed if you build
# something on PostgREST.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=<service-role key - server side only, never shipped>

# --- outbound email (musanga/mailer.py) ------------------------------------
# Without this, every quote, agreement and RFP invite goes out through
# Supabase Auth's magic-link mailer: no setup, but 2 emails/hour on the free
# tier and the from-address is Supabase's, not Musanga's. Fine for a demo,
# not for inviting five transporters to one RFP at once.
#
# Set RESEND_API_KEY to switch every outbound invite to Resend instead - see
# musanga/mailer.py for the exact fallback order. Get the key from
# https://resend.com/api-keys once signed in.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#
# Resend's shared sender (the default if this is unset) only delivers to the
# email the Resend account itself was signed up with - fine for testing,
# useless for real transporters. Sending to anyone else needs a domain
# verified in Resend (Domains -> Add Domain -> the DNS records it prints),
# and this set to an address on it.
# RESEND_FROM=Musanga <quotes@musanga.com>
#
# GET /api/health reports which mailer is actually active ("resend" or
# "supabase") without ever showing the key - check it after setting this.
